hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1464.1","Malik related to me from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"1464.2","Malik related to me from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"1465.1",""
"1465.2",""
"1466.1","Malik related to me from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman that a man in the time of Aban ibn Uthman's amirate freed all of his slaves and did not have other property than them. Aban ibn Uthman took charge of the slaves and they were divided into three groups. Then he drew lots on the basis that which ever group drew the dead man's arrow would be free. The arrow fell to one of the thirds"
"1466.2","Malik related to me from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman that a man in the time of Aban ibn Uthman's amirate freed all of his slaves and did not have other property than them. Aban ibn Uthman took charge of the slaves and they were divided into three groups. Then he drew lots on the basis that which ever group drew the dead man's arrow would be free. The arrow fell to one of the thirds"
"1467.1",""
"1467.2","Mālik narrated to me that it reached him that a man from the Anṣār, from the Banū al-Ḥārith ibn al-Khazraj, gave charity to his parents. Then they died, and their son inherited the wealth, which was date palms. He asked the Messenger of Allāh, peace be upon him, about that, and he said: \"You have been rewarded for your charity, and take it as your inheritance.\""
"1468.1",""
"1468.2","Malik related to me from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"1469.1","Malik related to me that he had heard that a slave-girl came to Umar ibn al-Khattab (who had been beaten by her master with a red hot iron) and he set her free. Malik said"
"1469.2","Malik related to me that he had heard that a slave-girl came to Umar ibn al-Khattab (who had been beaten by her master with a red hot iron) and he set her free. Malik said"
"1470.1","Malik related to me from Hilal ibn Usama from Ata ibn Yasar that Umar ibn al-Hakam said"
"1470.2","Malik related to me from Hilal ibn Usama from Ata ibn Yasar that Umar ibn al-Hakam said"
"1471.1","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud that one of the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah"
"1471.2","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud that one of the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah"
"1472.1","Malik related to me that he had heard that al-Maqburi said that Abu Hurayra was asked whether a man who had to free a slave"
"1472.2","Malik related to me that he had heard that al-Maqburi said that Abu Hurayra was asked whether a man who had to free a slave"
"1473.1","Malik related to me that he had heard that Fadala ibn Ubayd al- Ansari who was one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah"
"1473.2","Malik related to me that he had heard that Fadala ibn Ubayd al- Ansari who was one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah"
"1474.1","Malik related to me that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Umar was asked whether a slave could be bought on the specific condition that it was to be used to fulfil the obligation of freeing a slave"
"1474.2","Malik related to me that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Umar was asked whether a slave could be bought on the specific condition that it was to be used to fulfil the obligation of freeing a slave"
"1475.1","Malik related to me from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Amra al-Ansari that his mother had wanted to make a bequest"
"1475.2","Malik related to me from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Amra al-Ansari that his mother had wanted to make a bequest"
"1476.1","Mālik related that it reached him that Sa‘īd ibn al-Musayyab was asked about the pre-emption right, whether there was any Sunnah concerning it. He said: Yes, the pre-emption right is in houses and lands, and it only occurs between partners."
"1476.2","Mālik related to me, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sa‘īd ibn al-Musayyab, that ‘Uthmān ibn ‘Affān said: Whoever grants a gift to his young child who has not yet reached the age of taking possession of his gift, and he announces this and witnesses it, then it is valid, even if his father manages it for him."
"1477.1",""
"1477.2","Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from A'isha"
"1478.1",""
"1478.2","Malik related to me from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar freed an illegitimate child and its mother"
"1479.1","Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha"
"1479.2","Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha"
"1480.1","Malik related to me from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that A'isha umm al-muminin wanted to buy a slave-girl and set her free. Her people said"
"1480.2","Malik related to me from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that A'isha umm al-muminin wanted to buy a slave-girl and set her free. Her people said"
"1481.1","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Amra bint Abd ar- Rahman that Barira came asking the help of A'isha"
"1481.2","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Amra bint Abd ar- Rahman that Barira came asking the help of A'isha"
"1482.1","Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"1482.2","Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"1483.1","Malik said that it was not permissible for a slave to buy himself from his master on the provision that he could give the wala' to whomever he wished as the wala' was for the one who set him free"
"1483.2","Malik said that it was not permissible for a slave to buy himself from his master on the provision that he could give the wala' to whomever he wished as the wala' was for the one who set him free"
"1484.1","Malik related to me that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab was asked who had the wala' of the children whom a slave had by a free woman. Said said"
"1484.2","Malik related to me that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab was asked who had the wala' of the children whom a slave had by a free woman. Said said"
"1485.1","Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn al- Harith ibn Hisham that his father told him that al-Asi ibn Hisham had died and left three sons"
"1485.2","Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn al- Harith ibn Hisham that his father told him that al-Asi ibn Hisham had died and left three sons"
"1486.1","Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm that his father told him that he was sitting with Aban ibn Uthman"
"1486.2","Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm that his father told him that he was sitting with Aban ibn Uthman"
"1487.1","Malik related to me that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab spoke about a man who died and left three sons and left mawali whom he had freed. Then two of his sons died and left children. He said"
"1487.2","Malik related to me that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab spoke about a man who died and left three sons and left mawali whom he had freed. Then two of his sons died and left children. He said"
"1488.1",""
"1488.2","Malik related to me that he had asked Ibn Shihab about a slave who was released. He said"
